# Earthcall — ignore rules.
#
# Before this file existed the repository tracked 2,481 MB, of which 7.7 MB was
# hand-written source. The rest was build output, compiled binaries, debug
# bundles, a committed virtualenv, and 1.9 GB of runtime save data. Everything
# listed here is REGENERATED from the sources, or is user data that was never
# source in the first place.

# --- macOS -------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*

# --- C++ build output --------------------------------------------------------
build/
*.o
*.d
*.dSYM/
*.gch
*.pch

# Compiled binaries. The app and every test target land in sight-cpp/ next to
# the Makefile; 32 of them were tracked, at ~6.5 MB each.
sight-cpp/earthcall
sight-cpp/src/earthcall
sight-cpp/*_test
sight-cpp/test_parse
sight-cpp/test_parse2
sight-cpp/webgpu_smoke
sight-cpp/webgpu_mesh
sight-cpp/webgpu_renderer
sight-cpp/webgpu_window
sight-cpp/tests/*_test
TestLabAI/testlab_ai
# ...but keep the sources that build them.
!*.cpp
!*.hpp
!*.h

# wgpu-native: the static .a is committed on purpose; the .dylib is unused.
sight-cpp/third_party/wgpu/lib/libwgpu_native.dylib

# --- Runtime output ----------------------------------------------------------
# Save games are USER DATA produced by running the program, not source. They
# were the single largest thing in the repository (1.9 GB across 330 files,
# with two individual saves over 100 MB each). Test fixtures belong in
# sight-cpp/tests/fixtures/, which is deliberately not ignored.
sight-cpp/saves/
sight-cpp/save.json
sight-cpp/debug_log.txt
sight-cpp/run.log
sight-cpp/imgui.ini
sight-cpp/scratch/

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
